==Old English==

===Etymology===
From Germanic ''*waroþō'', an extension of a stem-verb ''*wāro-'' ‘be on guard’ (OE [[warian]]).  Cognate with Old High German [[warta]] ‘watch’ (German [[Warte]] ‘watchtower’), Old Saxon [[warda]] (Middle Dutch [[warde]]), Old Norse [[varða]] ‘cairn’.

